session:pr770Summary a agp:TranscriptSummary ;
    agp:summaryText "Issue #743 (second sub-issue of epic #741, SPARQL SERVICE federation) needed a way to turn a SERVICE clause's inner Vec<QueryComponent> back into SPARQL query text to forward to a remote endpoint. Rather than guessing at the subset of QueryComponent/Expression/PropertyPath actually reachable inside a SERVICE body today, the new sparql_parser/src/service_text.rs module handles every variant of all three enums, on the reasoning that an unhandled variant silently producing wrong/incomplete text would be a worse failure mode than a slightly larger module. Operator and property-path precedence is handled by parenthesizing every binary/unary operand and non-atomic path operand liberally, rather than reproducing SPARQL's full precedence grammar -- valid, round-trippable SPARQL was the bar (per the issue), not minimal/pretty output. While wiring up triple-pattern leaves to reuse the existing crate::explain::render_triple_pattern/render_term (per the issue's explicit instruction not to duplicate that logic), discovered render_term's Constant arm called GraphElement::to_string() directly, which is not round-trippable: a plain string literal rendered as (text) with no quotes, and a blank node as _:(id) with parentheses that are not valid BLANK_NODE_LABEL syntax. Added render_graph_element to explain.rs with correct literal escaping/typed-literal/boolean/numeric syntax and _:bN blank-node syntax, and repointed render_term at it -- this incidentally fixes every other existing caller of render_term/render_triple_pattern (mostly EXPLAIN/profile debug-label output), not just the new serializer. A CI Docs-job failure (rustdoc::private_intra_doc_links, since render_triple_pattern/render_term are pub(crate) not pub) was found and fixed after the initial PR push: the module doc comment's [`...`] markdown links to those two private functions were changed to plain code-font text." ;
    agp:reasoningFor ghpull:770 ;
    agp:decisionPoint session:pr770Decision ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy session:pr770 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo session:claudeSonnet5 .

session:pr770Decision a agp:Decision ;
    agp:summaryText "Render every QueryComponent/Expression/PropertyPath variant (full enum coverage) rather than only the subset known to be reachable inside a SERVICE body today, and always parenthesize operator/path operands rather than reproducing SPARQL's precedence grammar." ;
    agp:alternative "A narrower renderer covering only BGP/FILTER/OPTIONAL/UNION/property-paths (the issue's explicitly-named minimum) was considered, but rejected: an unhandled QueryComponent/Expression variant reached via some future executor change would silently produce wrong or truncated SPARQL text rather than a compile-time match error, which is a worse failure mode than the small amount of extra code needed to cover the full enums now. Likewise, reproducing SPARQL's operator/path precedence table to emit minimally-parenthesized text was rejected as unnecessary complexity given the issue's own acceptance bar is round-tripping, not textual fidelity." .
